The Bot page (public/js/bots.js, bots-settings.js, bots-usage.js, bot-mentions.js,
bot-avatar.js; server/bots/; server/routes/bots.js)

  Source:   DS Bot, https://github.com/Fei2411/DS-Bot
            Copyright its contributors.
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0, https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

  What was taken: design, not code or art. The Bot page follows DS Bot's
  published design — a main bot ("Chief", Chief of Staff) that creates the other
  bots and the group chats when asked; group chats with an admin that answers a
  message calling nobody and hands work on with "@Name"; a member called that way
  doing the work in its own context for that group and posting back, the bot that
  asked then answering what came back; one shared reading of "@Name" for the
  server and the page (longest name first; an address or a code span is no call);
  a bot's own memory and a group memory read only in that group, as data and not
  as instructions; a details panel (model, instructions, memory, usage) and a
  settings page with usage by time, by bot and by model; "Thought it through" for
  a turn's reasoning.

  What was not taken: none of DS Bot's source code, prompts, wording or artwork.
  Every line of the Bot page is written for this app, and a bot's face is one of
  Synapsez's own pixel creatures (public/js/mascots/), not one of DS Bot's
  characters. Where this app departs from DS Bot — a hard ceiling on hand-offs per
  message, one streamed request per group round, entries in a database rather than
  Markdown files, no per-bot browser — is said in server/bots/rounds.js and
  server/bots/memory.js.

  This is a modified work in the sense of the licence's section 4 only so far as a
  design can be one; it is not DS Bot and is not endorsed by its authors.
